{"id":"046bdb8cc2cee29d233964bb77fe6fd37cfe4aa3","axis":"silent","repo":"huggingface/transformers","sha":"046bdb8cc2cee29d233964bb77fe6fd37cfe4aa3","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/source/en/_toctree.yml","lines":["@@ -1451,6 +1451,8 @@","         title: Inkling","       - local: model_doc/inkling2","         title: Inkling2","+      - local: model_doc/inkling2_loop","+        title: Inkling2Loop","       - local: model_doc/instructblip","         title: InstructBLIP","       - local: model_doc/instructblipvideo"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/source/en/model_doc/inkling2.md","lines":["@@ -114,6 +114,9 @@ print(processor.decode(outputs[0][input_len:], skip_special_tokens=False))"," ## Notes"," "," - Attention runs in eager mode only, because every layer adds a relative position bias and a sink.","+- The short convolutions use fast GPU kernels when available: Hub kernels when loading with `use_kernels=True`,","+  otherwise the [causal-conv1d](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/causal-conv1d) package if installed","+  (`pip install causal-conv1d`). Without them, they fall back to a slower PyTorch implementation."," "," ## Inkling2Config"," "],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/source/en/model_doc/inkling2_loop.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,216 @@","+<!--Copyright 2026 the HuggingFace Team. All rights reserved.","+","+Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");","+you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.","+You may obtain a copy of the License at","+","+    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0","+","+Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software","+distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,","+WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.","+See the License for the specific language governing permissions and","+limitations under the License.","+","+","+⚠️ Note that this file is in Markdown but contains specific syntax for our doc-builder (similar to MDX) that may not be rendered properly in your Markdown viewer.","+","+-->","+*This model was contributed to Hugging Face Transformers on 2026-11-21.*","+","+# Inkling 2 Mini","+","+[Inkling 2 Mini](https://huggingface.co/collections/thinkingmachines/inkling-2) is a multimodal model from [Thinking Machines Lab](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines) that accepts text and image inputs and generates text outputs. It is based on [Inkling 2 Small](./inkling2) but has only 24 decoder layers instead of 48. The lower layer count is compensated for by a looping mechanism in which layers 6 to 17 run three times. Information is shared between loop passes through a learned message-passing mechanism that mixes the residuals of the previous pass into the attention and mixture-of-experts inputs of each loop layer. The decoder has a hidden size of 2304 and routes each token to 8 of 128 experts. The image encoder, tokenizer and processor are identical to those of Inkling 2 Small.","+","+Inkling 2 Mini comes with an additional [research checkpoint](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/TML-d24-varloop-research) that supports a variable number of loop passes. The architecture is identical to the main Inkling 2 Mini model. The number of loop passes can be adjusted to trade off speed against quality. Fewer passes are faster, while more passes improve quality.","+","+Both checkpoints contain NVFP4 and MXFP8 quantized layers that Transformers dequantizes when loading the model.","+","+**Checkpoints**","+","+- [Inkling 2 Mini](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini)","+- [Inkling 2 Mini varloop research](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/TML-d24-varloop-research)","+","+## Resources","+","+- [Thinking Machines Blog](https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/inkling-2-mini/)","+- [Hugging Face Blog](https://huggingface.co/blog/inkling2mini)","+","+<hfoptions id=\"usage\">","+<hfoption id=\"Pipeline\">","+","+```python","+import torch","+","+from transformers import pipeline","+","+pipe = pipeline(","+    \"image-text-to-text\", model=\"thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini\", dtype=torch.bfloat16, device_map=\"auto\"","+)","+","+messages = [","+    {","+        \"role\": \"user\",","+        \"content\": [","+            {","+                \"type\": \"image\",","+                \"image\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/huggingface/documentation-images/resolve/main/pipeline-cat-chonk.jpeg\",","+            },","+            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"What animal is in this image, and where is it?\"},","+        ],","+    },","+]","+","+output = pipe(messages, max_new_tokens=1024, return_full_text=False, skip_special_tokens=False)","+print(output[0][\"generated_text\"])","+# <|message_model|><|content_thinking|>The user is asking about an animal in an image. Let me","+# analyze what I see: a small wild feline with thick, fluffy fur dusted with snow, short legs, a","+# broad face, and black stripes/spots.","+# ...","+# <|end_message|><|message_model|><|content_text|>The animal appears to be a Pallas’s cat (manul) —","+# a small, bear-like wild cat with thick speckled/striped fur. It’s standing on snow inside what","+# looks like a zoo or wildlife enclosure, with snow-covered birch/log branches and a chain-link","+# fence in the background.<|end_message|><|content_model_end_sampling|>","+```","+","+</hfoption>","+<hfoption id=\"AutoModel\">","+","+```python","+import torch","+","+from transformers import AutoModelForMultimodalLM, AutoProcessor","+","+model_id = \"thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini\"","+processor = AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(model_id)","+model = AutoModelForMultimodalLM.from_pretrained(model_id, dtype=torch.bfloat16, device_map=\"auto\")","+","+messages = [","+    {","+        \"role\": \"user\",","+        \"content\": [","+            {","+                \"type\": \"image\",","+                \"image\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/huggingface/documentation-images/resolve/main/pipeline-cat-chonk.jpeg\",","+            },","+            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"What animal is in this image, and where is it?\"},","+        ],","+    },","+]","+","+inputs = processor.apply_chat_template(","+    messages,","+    tokenize=True,","+    add_generation_prompt=True,","+    return_dict=True,","+    return_tensors=\"pt\",","+).to(model.device)","+input_len = inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[-1]","+","+outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=1024)","+print(processor.decode(outputs[0][input_len:], skip_special_tokens=False))","+# <|message_model|><|content_thinking|>The user is asking what animal is in the image and where it","+# is. Let me analyze the image.","+# ...","+# <|end_message|><|message_model|><|content_text|>The animal appears to be a Pallas’s cat (manul), a","+# stocky small wild cat with thick, snow-dusted fur. It is standing on snow, likely inside a zoo or","+# wildlife enclosure — you can see birch/aspen-like posts and chain-link fencing in the","+# background.<|end_message|><|content_model_end_sampling|>","+```","+","+</hfoption>","+","+<hfoption id=\"AutoModel Variable Loops\">","+","+```python","+import torch","+","+from transformers import AutoModelForMultimodalLM, AutoProcessor","+","+model_id = \"thinkingmachines/TML-d24-varloop-research\"","+processor = AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(model_id)","+model = AutoModelForMultimodalLM.from_pretrained(","+    model_id,","+    dtype=torch.bfloat16,","+    device_map=\"auto\",","+    text_config={\"loop_num_passes\": 3},  # number of loop passes, must be at least 1","+)","+","+messages = [","+    {","+        \"role\": \"user\",","+        \"content\": [","+            {","+                \"type\": \"image\",","+                \"image\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/huggingface/documentation-images/resolve/main/pipeline-cat-chonk.jpeg\",","+            },","+            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"What animal is in this image, and where is it?\"},","+        ],","+    },","+]","+","+inputs = processor.apply_chat_template(","+    messages,","+    tokenize=True,","+    add_generation_prompt=True,","+    return_dict=True,","+    return_tensors=\"pt\",","+).to(model.device)","+input_len = inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[-1]","+","+outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=1024)","+print(processor.decode(outputs[0][input_len:], skip_special_tokens=False))","+# <|message_model|><|content_thinking|>We need answer image question. Need identify animal and where","+# is it.","+# ...","+# <|end_message|><|message_model|><|content_text|>The animal is a Pallas’s cat (a.k.a. Manul), a","+# stocky, densely furred small wild cat. It’s in the snow outdoors in a cold setting—likely a winter","+# enclosure/habitat—standing/walking on snow at the center of the","+# image.<|end_message|><|content_model_end_sampling|>","+```","+","+</hfoption>","+","+</hfoptions>","+","+## Notes","+","+- Attention runs in eager mode only because every layer adds a relative position bias and a sink.","+- The short convolutions use fast GPU kernels when available: Hub kernels when loading with `use_kernels=True`,","+  otherwise the [causal-conv1d](https://github.com/Dao-AILab/causal-conv1d) package if installed","+  (`pip install causal-conv1d`). Without them, they fall back to a slower PyTorch implementation.","+- Every pass through the loop layers keeps its own keys, values and convolution states, so the cache has one layer per layer visit (48 for the released checkpoint).","+- `output_hidden_states` and `output_attentions` return one entry per layer visit.","+","+## Inkling2LoopConfig","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2LoopConfig","+","+## Inkling2LoopTextConfig","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2LoopTextConfig","+","+## Inkling2LoopPreTrainedModel","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2LoopPreTrainedModel","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2LoopTextModel","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2LoopTextModel","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2LoopForCausalLM","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2LoopForCausalLM","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2LoopModel","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2LoopModel","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2LoopForConditionalGeneration","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2LoopForConditionalGeneration","+    - forward"],"additions":216,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/conversion_mapping.py","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,9 @@","     ErnieFuseAndSplitTextVisionExperts,","     GroupWeightRename,","     Inkling2IndexOffsetWeightRename,","+    Inkling2LoopDequantizeExperts,","+    Inkling2LoopMergeMessageQueries,","+    Inkling2UnpadVocab,","     Interleave,","     LayerPairCollapse,","     MergeModulelist,","@@ -297,6 +300,11 @@ def _build_checkpoint_conversion_mapping():","         ],","         \"inkling2\": [","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.unembed\\.\", target_patterns=r\"lm_head.\"),","+            WeightConverter(","+                source_patterns=r\"lm_head\\.weight\",","+                target_patterns=r\"lm_head.weight\",","+                operations=[Inkling2UnpadVocab()],","+            ),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.language_model.\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.visual\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.vision_tower.\"),","             WeightRenaming(","@@ -344,6 +352,11 @@ def _build_checkpoint_conversion_mapping():","         ],","         \"inkling2_text\": [","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.unembed\\.\", target_patterns=r\"lm_head.\"),","+            WeightConverter(","+                source_patterns=r\"lm_head\\.weight\",","+                target_patterns=r\"lm_head.weight\",","+                operations=[Inkling2UnpadVocab()],","+            ),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"embed\\.weight\", target_patterns=r\"embed_tokens.weight\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"embed_norm\\.\", target_patterns=r\"embed_tokens.embed_norm.\"),","@@ -363,12 +376,23 @@ def _build_checkpoint_conversion_mapping():","             ),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"mlp.gate.bias\", target_patterns=r\"mlp.gate.e_score_correction_bias\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"\\.attn\\.\", target_patterns=r\".self_attn.\"),","-            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wq_du\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.q_proj\"),","-            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wk_dv\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.k_proj\"),","-            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wv_dv\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.v_proj\"),","-            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wr_du\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.r_proj\"),","-            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wo_ud\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.o_proj\"),","-            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.gate_attn\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.gate_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wq_du\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.q_proj.linear\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wk_dv\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.k_proj.linear\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wv_dv\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.v_proj.linear\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.k_sconv\\.\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.k_proj.sconv.\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.v_sconv\\.\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.v_proj.sconv.\"),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.rel_logits_proj\\.\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.relative_position_bias.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wr_du\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.relative_position_bias.linear\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.q_l2_clip\\.\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.q_proj.norm.\"),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.rel_l2_clip\\.\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.relative_position_bias.norm.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.wo_ud\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.o_proj.linear\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.gate_attn\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.o_proj.gate_proj\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"self_attn\\.attn_sink_proj\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.sink_proj\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn_sconv\\.\", target_patterns=r\"post_attention_convolution.\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"mlp_sconv\\.\", target_patterns=r\"post_mlp_convolution.\"),","@@ -2627,6 +2651,62 @@ def _build_checkpoint_conversion_mapping():","         ),","     ]"," ","+    mapping[\"inkling2_loop\"] = mapping[\"inkling2\"].copy()","+    # Temporary: the original Inkling2Loop checkpoints store NVFP4 and MXFP8 experts. They are dequantized on load and","+    # replace the Inkling2 expert transforms, which keep MXFP8 experts quantized.","+    inkling2_loop_experts = [","+        WeightConverter(","+            source_patterns=[","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w13_weight\",","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w13_weight_scale\",","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w13_weight_amax\",","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w13_weight_outer_scale_denominator\",","+            ],","+            target_patterns=r\"mlp.experts.gate_up_proj\",","+            operations=[Inkling2LoopDequantizeExperts(), Interleave(dim=1)],","+        ),","+        WeightConverter(","+            source_patterns=[","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w2_weight\",","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w2_weight_scale\",","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w2_weight_amax\",","+                r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w2_weight_outer_scale_denominator\",","+            ],","+            target_patterns=r\"mlp.experts.down_proj\",","+            operations=[Inkling2LoopDequantizeExperts()],","+        ),","+    ]","+    inkling2_text = [","+        transform","+        for transform in mapping[\"inkling2_text\"]","+        if not transform._original_source_patterns[0].startswith(r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w\")","+    ]","+    mapping[\"inkling2_loop_text\"] = [","+        WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"controllers\\.attn\\.\", target_patterns=r\"q_message_gate.\"),","+        WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"controllers\\.k\\.\", target_patterns=r\"k_message_gate.\"),","+        WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"controllers\\.v\\.\", target_patterns=r\"v_message_gate.\"),","+        WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"controllers\\.mlp\\.\", target_patterns=r\"mlp_message_gate.\"),","+        WeightRenaming(","+            source_patterns=r\"_message_gate\\.down_weight\", target_patterns=r\"_message_gate.down_proj.weight\"","+        ),","+        WeightRenaming(","+            source_patterns=r\"_message_gate\\.gain_weight\", target_patterns=r\"_message_gate.message_gate_proj.weight\"","+        ),","+        WeightRenaming(","+            source_patterns=r\"_message_gate\\.forget_weight\", target_patterns=r\"_message_gate.forget_gate_proj.weight\"","+        ),","+        # The original checkpoint stores two (2 * num_loop_layers, hidden_size) query parameters:","+        # - middle_cycle_cross_pass_queries: the query and mlp queries of each loop layer","+        # - middle_cycle_cross_pass_kv_queries: the key and value queries of each loop layer","+        # We merge them into a single (num_loop_layers, 4, hidden_size) query param.","+        WeightConverter(","+            source_patterns=[r\"middle_cycle_cross_pass_queries\", r\"middle_cycle_cross_pass_kv_queries\"],","+            target_patterns=r\"message_input.query\",","+            operations=[Inkling2LoopMergeMessageQueries()],","+        ),","+        *inkling2_loop_experts,","+    ] + inkling2_text","+","     for model_type, base_pattern in _MODEL_TO_CONVERSION_PATTERN.items():","         if model_type in mapping:","             continue"],"additions":86,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/core_model_loading.py","lines":["@@ -769,6 +769,119 @@ def reverse_op(self) -> ConversionOps:","         return ErnieFuseAndSplitTextVisionExperts(stack_dim=self.stack_dim, concat_dim=self.concat_dim)"," "," ","+class Inkling2LoopDequantizeExperts(ConversionOps):","+    r\"\"\"","+    Temporary op that dequantizes the NVFP4 and MXFP8 expert weights of the original Inkling2Loop checkpoints to the","+    dtype of the model param, until these formats can be loaded quantized.","+","+    - NVFP4 (`amax` present): two E2M1 codes per byte (even element in the low nibble), one float8 scale per 16 values","+      and a per-expert factor `amax / outer_scale_denominator`.","+    - MXFP8: float8 values with one power-of-two scale `2 ** (scale - 127)` per 32 values.","+    \"\"\"","+","+    E2M1_VALUES = (0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 6.0, -0.0, -0.5, -1.0, -1.5, -2.0, -3.0, -4.0, -6.0)","+    EXPERTS_PER_CHUNK = 8","+","+    @torch.no_grad()","+    def convert(self, input_dict, source_patterns, target_patterns, model=None, full_layer_name=None, **kwargs):","+        tensors = {key: value[0] if isinstance(value, list) else value for key, value in input_dict.items()}","+        if len(tensors) == 1:","+            return {target_patterns[0]: next(iter(tensors.values()))}","+        weight, scale, amax, denominator = (tensors.get(pattern) for pattern in source_patterns)","+","+        # Without a quantizer, the loader casts all sources to the param dtype, but don't rely on it","+        try:","+            dtype = model.get_parameter(full_layer_name).dtype","+        except (AttributeError, TypeError):","+            dtype = torch.bfloat16","+        num_experts, rows = weight.shape[:2]","+        columns = weight.shape[2] * 2 if amax is not None else weight.shape[2]","+        output = torch.empty(num_experts, rows, columns, dtype=dtype, device=weight.device)","+        if amax is not None:","+            e2m1_values = torch.tensor(self.E2M1_VALUES, device=weight.device)","+            byte = torch.arange(256, device=weight.device)","+            byte_to_values = torch.stack((e2m1_values[byte & 0xF], e2m1_values[byte >> 4]), dim=-1)","+            expert_factor = amax.float() / denominator.float()","+        for start in range(0, num_experts, self.EXPERTS_PER_CHUNK):","+            experts = slice(start, start + self.EXPERTS_PER_CHUNK)","+            block_scale = scale[experts].float()","+            if amax is None:","+                values = weight[experts].float().view(*block_scale.shape, 32)","+                values = values * torch.exp2(block_scale - 127)[..., None]","+            else:","+                codes = weight[experts].to(torch.uint8).long()","+                values = byte_to_values[codes].view(*block_scale.shape, 16) * block_scale[..., None]","+                values = values * expert_factor[experts, None, None, None]","+            output[experts] = values.reshape(-1, rows, columns).to(dtype)","+        return {target_patterns[0]: output}","+","+    @property","+    def reverse_op(self) -> ConversionOps:","+        return self","+","+","+class Inkling2LoopMergeMessageQueries(ConversionOps):","+    r\"\"\"","+    Merges the message queries of the original Inkling2Loop checkpoints into one `(num_loop_layers, 4, hidden_size)`","+    tensor, or splits them back with `inverse=True`. The checkpoints store them as two","+    `(2 * num_loop_layers, hidden_size)` tensors: the query and MLP queries of each loop layer, then its key and value","+    queries. The merged tensor holds the query, key, value and MLP queries of each loop layer, in that order.","+    \"\"\"","+","+    def __init__(self, inverse: bool = False):","+        self.inverse = inverse","+","+    @torch.no_grad","+    def convert(self, input_dict, source_patterns, target_patterns, **kwargs):","+        if self.inverse:","+            tensor = next(iter(input_dict.values()))","+            tensor = tensor[0] if isinstance(tensor, list) else tensor","+            queries = tensor[:, [0, 3]].flatten(0, 1)","+            kv_queries = tensor[:, 1:3].flatten(0, 1)","+            return {target_patterns[0]: queries.contiguous(), target_patterns[1]: kv_queries.contiguous()}","+","+        queries, kv_queries = (input_dict[pattern] for pattern in source_patterns)","+        queries = queries[0] if isinstance(queries, list) else queries","+        kv_queries = kv_queries[0] if isinstance(kv_queries, list) else kv_queries","+        # (num_loop_layers, 2, hidden_size): [query, mlp] and [key, value] of each loop layer","+        queries = queries.unflatten(0, (-1, 2))","+        kv_queries = kv_queries.unflatten(0, (-1, 2))","+        return {target_patterns[0]: torch.cat([queries[:, :1], kv_queries, queries[:, 1:]], dim=1)}","+","+    @property","+    def reverse_op(self) -> ConversionOps:","+        return Inkling2LoopMergeMessageQueries(inverse=not self.inverse)","+","+","+class Inkling2UnpadVocab(ConversionOps):","+    r\"\"\"","+    Drops the padded rows of the Inkling2 unembedding, which checkpoints store padded to `vocab_size`, keeping the first","+    `unpadded_vocab_size` rows. With `inverse=True`, appends zero rows to pad it back to `vocab_size`.","+    \"\"\"","+","+    def __init__(self, inverse: bool = False):","+        self.inverse = inverse","+","+    @torch.no_grad","+    def convert(","+        self, input_dict, source_patterns, target_patterns, config=None, model=None, full_layer_name=None, **kwargs","+    ):","+        tensor = next(iter(input_dict.values()))","+        tensor = tensor[0] if isinstance(tensor, list) else tensor","+        text_config = config.get_text_config()","+        if self.inverse:","+            padding = tensor.new_zeros(text_config.vocab_size - tensor.shape[0], *tensor.shape[1:])","+            tensor = torch.cat([tensor, padding], dim=0)","+        else:","+            dtype = model.get_parameter(full_layer_name).dtype","+            tensor = tensor[: text_config.unpadded_vocab_size].to(dtype).contiguous()","+        return {target_patterns[0]: tensor}","+","+    @property","+    def reverse_op(self) -> ConversionOps:","+        return Inkling2UnpadVocab(inverse=not self.inverse)","+","+"," def process_target_pattern(pattern: str) -> tuple[str, str | None]:","     \"\"\"","     Process a target pattern for reverse mapping (when targets become sources)."],"additions":113,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/models/__init__.py","lines":["@@ -248,6 +248,7 @@","     from .informer import *","     from .inkling import *","     from .inkling2 import *","+    from .inkling2_loop import *","     from .instructblip import *","     from .instructblipvideo import *","     from .internlm3 import *"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/models/auto/auto_mappings.py","lines":["@@ -345,6 +345,8 @@","         (\"imagegpt\", \"ImageGPTConfig\"),","         (\"informer\", \"InformerConfig\"),","         (\"inkling2\", \"Inkling2Config\"),","+        (\"inkling2_loop\", \"Inkling2LoopConfig\"),","+        (\"inkling2_loop_text\", \"Inkling2LoopTextConfig\"),","         (\"inkling2_text\", \"Inkling2TextConfig\"),","         (\"inkling2_vision\", \"Inkling2VisionConfig\"),","         (\"inkling_audio\", \"InklingAudioConfig\"),","@@ -957,6 +959,7 @@","         (\"idefics3_vision\", \"idefics3\"),","         (\"idefics_perciever\", \"idefics\"),","         (\"idefics_vision\", \"idefics\"),","+        (\"inkling2_loop_text\", \"inkling2_loop\"),","         (\"inkling2_text\", \"inkling2\"),","         (\"inkling2_vision\", \"inkling2\"),","         (\"inkling_audio\", \"i